  "content": {
    "id": "coordinate-inverse-distance-r36-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Calculate the values of $k$ if the distance between $(k,k-1)$ and $(-1,4)$ is exactly $5\\sqrt{2}$ units.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$k=6$ or $-2$. Square the distance equation and factorise the resulting quadratic.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{(-1-k)^2+(4-(k-1))^2}&=5\\sqrt{2}\\\\(-1-k)^2+(5-k)^2&=50\\\\1+2k+k^2+25-10k+k^2&=50\\\\2k^2-8k+26&=50\\\\2k^2-8k-24&=0\\\\k^2-4k-12&=0\\end{align*}$$PSF: Product $=-12$, Sum $=-4$, Factors $=2$ and $-6$.$$\\begin{align*}(k+2)(k-6)&=0\\\\k&=-2\\text{ or }6\\end{align*}$$Check $k=6$: $\\sqrt{(-7)^2+(-1)^2}=\\sqrt{50}$. Check $k=-2$: $\\sqrt{1^2+7^2}=\\sqrt{50}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
